WEBVTT

00:47.810 --> 00:51.900
The world was just a bubble born at the bottom of the water

00:53.350 --> 00:53.980
Bubble?

00:55.230 --> 00:55.850
Yes

00:56.600 --> 01:00.900
The bottom is like the past, the surface is the future

01:02.850 --> 01:05.400
Bubbles gradually expand as they float up

01:06.400 --> 01:07.500
finally burst

01:10.350 --> 01:13.150
We're living in a bubble after it's broken

01:16.440 --> 01:20.500
So, from the other bubbles we see

01:20.500 --> 01:23.650
It's called Parallel world, that is, parallel world

01:24.100 --> 01:25.520
Parallel world?

01:26.520 --> 01:28.770
It's a world with different choices

01:29.980 --> 01:34.150
But the closer the parallel world, the smaller the difference

01:34.900 --> 01:39.310
That is, the difference between whether you eat bread or rice in the morning

01:40.270 --> 01:43.900
So we may have unknowingly performed a parallel shift

01:45.270 --> 01:46.650
Parallel shift?

01:47.480 --> 01:49.440
It means move between parallel worlds

01:49.980 --> 01:50.980
Can it be moved?

01:51.600 --> 01:52.300
Actualy...

01:54.090 --> 01:55.440
Only the consciousness

01:56.900 --> 01:59.000
What you are looking for appears where you have found it

01:59.000 --> 02:01.100
You must have had this experience

02:01.940 --> 02:04.810
That is, misremembering or forgetting

02:05.350 --> 02:10.230
Most likely caused by an involuntary parallel shift

02:12.400 --> 02:15.980
These knowledge related to the parallel world

02:15.980 --> 02:18.810
That is the virtual science we're working on

02:21.810 --> 02:25.100
So how many parallel worlds are there?

02:25.650 --> 02:29.100
Well, it depends on how many times you choose

02:30.350 --> 02:31.350
We should go

02:32.980 --> 02:34.650
Mom must be hungry

02:37.400 --> 02:38.100
See

02:40.230 --> 02:42.980
Sorry, we're leaving

02:43.940 --> 02:44.850
You go to the store first...

02:49.650 --> 02:51.060
Yeah i got it

02:53.730 --> 02:54.480
See you later

02:57.980 --> 02:59.520
Yuno is passed away

03:01.230 --> 03:05.440
It jumped out during a walk and was hit by a car

03:08.060 --> 03:12.310
I was 7 years old when I made my first big choice

03:21.020 --> 03:26.940
To the one who loves you deeply

03:29.940 --> 03:31.310
I will take a pict

03:32.190 --> 03:34.230
Look at the camera and smile

03:36.270 --> 03:37.650
Ah sorry

03:57.940 --> 04:03.100
Yuno is the dog my grandfather raised when I was born

04:33.440 --> 04:34.230
Koyomi

04:35.980 --> 04:37.190
Grandpa

04:38.900 --> 04:41.230
You are here, thank you

04:44.270 --> 04:47.560
Yuno, Koyomi is here to see you

04:53.730 --> 04:55.350
Sorry Yuno

04:56.060 --> 04:58.150
I can't save you

05:00.150 --> 05:01.310
I'm really sorry

05:43.150 --> 05:43.980
What's happen

05:48.350 --> 05:49.190
Are you crying?

05:51.350 --> 05:52.230
I didn't cry

05:54.350 --> 05:55.480
Obviously crying

05:55.480 --> 05:56.730
I didn't cry

05:59.060 --> 06:00.150
You are crying

06:01.150 --> 06:01.850
Shut up

06:04.810 --> 06:05.850
I want to see Yuno

06:06.940 --> 06:07.730
Yuno ?

06:09.560 --> 06:11.350
My grandfather's dog

06:12.400 --> 06:13.400
Can't you see her?

06:15.190 --> 06:18.690
I can't see because it's dead

06:20.350 --> 06:22.650
Yuno is dead

06:22.650 --> 06:24.650
I will never see her again

06:48.770 --> 06:49.940
Hey, come with me

06:54.980 --> 06:56.730
Wait, where are you going?

06:57.060 --> 06:59.350
Shh, mom will find out

07:01.980 --> 07:04.230
Does your mother work here?

07:05.020 --> 07:07.270
Yeah that's why i'm here

07:08.560 --> 07:09.400
True

07:17.560 --> 07:20.100
Wow what is that ?

07:20.690 --> 07:21.810
IP capsule

07:23.770 --> 07:26.190
When you lie down on that, you can go to the parallel world

07:26.560 --> 07:28.770
Eh, parallel world?

07:29.730 --> 07:31.770
It's a world with different choices

07:33.690 --> 07:36.190
For example, are the rice ball stuffed with mayonnaise or tuna?

07:36.650 --> 07:37.850
There will be a small difference

07:39.730 --> 07:42.400
Maybe you can use it to go to the world where Yuno is still alive

07:49.190 --> 07:50.230
I will close it

07:51.020 --> 07:53.900
Wait, what should i do next?

07:54.770 --> 07:57.100
Wish it and keep thinking of Yuno

07:57.730 --> 07:58.520
Wish?

07:59.600 --> 08:02.690
My mom said it's important to believe your wish

08:03.480 --> 08:07.350
Only those who never give up can change the world

08:08.690 --> 08:09.690
Ah, hey!

08:15.480 --> 08:16.060
Good

08:19.190 --> 08:21.980
Does she know how to operate it?

08:23.980 --> 08:26.730
Oh, I can only try

08:31.190 --> 08:33.980
I want to see Yuno, I want to see Yuno

08:34.520 --> 08:37.600
Yuno, Yuno, Yuno!

08:47.350 --> 08:48.440
Where is it?

08:51.600 --> 08:52.190
Yuno?

08:57.600 --> 08:58.400
Yuno!

09:02.810 --> 09:03.730
Yuno!

09:06.190 --> 09:07.190
Yuno

09:10.350 --> 09:11.560
It's really you

09:12.940 --> 09:14.310
Stop it. Hey

09:15.310 --> 09:17.980
Hey Yuno, where are you going?

09:18.480 --> 09:20.480
Yuno, wait for me

09:28.150 --> 09:29.380
I'm back

09:29.980 --> 09:31.350
Or what i should say

09:33.440 --> 09:34.690
Ah sorry

09:41.560 --> 09:42.520
Welcome back

09:43.440 --> 09:46.190
Your clothes are in the room, go and change

09:47.230 --> 09:48.350
It's about to start

09:50.810 --> 09:51.520
What is going to start?

09:53.980 --> 09:56.150
Are you Shoudai?

09:57.020 --> 09:58.900
Yes, long time no see

10:00.940 --> 10:01.400
Koyomi

10:13.350 --> 10:14.350
Grandpa...

10:20.060 --> 10:23.400
Then Mayumi, see you tomorrow

10:23.770 --> 10:25.270
Thank you

10:25.480 --> 10:28.310
Even Koyomi cried for the first time

10:28.900 --> 10:31.900
Yasuto must be a really good grandfather

10:32.190 --> 10:32.850
Yes

10:46.190 --> 10:46.850
Yuno

10:55.100 --> 10:55.810
Koyomi

10:56.230 --> 10:59.600
Go to bed early, you have to get up early tomorrow

11:00.560 --> 11:01.400
Mother

11:03.100 --> 11:04.600
Can we sleep together tonight

11:15.940 --> 11:18.190
It hurts

11:19.190 --> 11:19.940
Huh?

11:22.270 --> 11:23.480
Where it is?

11:25.150 --> 11:27.020
Oh Koyomi you're awake already?

11:27.020 --> 11:28.230
Grandpa

11:29.350 --> 11:30.190
You are still alive?

11:30.190 --> 11:33.560
What do you mean, don't say such unlucky words

11:47.020 --> 11:48.940
It seems that I have returned to the original world

11:58.650 --> 11:59.600
What's wrong

12:02.310 --> 12:03.190
Nothing

12:03.650 --> 12:04.400
What about mom

12:04.810 --> 12:06.310
Already went to work

12:06.850 --> 12:07.560
That's it

12:08.060 --> 12:12.020
But grandpa was very happy to sleep with you last night

12:12.020 --> 12:12.690
Grandpa

12:17.350 --> 12:18.440
May you have a long life

12:19.060 --> 12:20.650
What happened to you

12:21.020 --> 12:24.350
Don't worry, grandpa's body is still strong

12:24.850 --> 12:27.650
Well, that's true

12:30.850 --> 12:32.230
Lets play again sometime

12:36.310 --> 12:40.440
The rabbit said to him, "Let's fire up, sir."

12:41.100 --> 12:44.100
The boy picked up many dead branches...

12:43.520 --> 12:44.100
Yo

12:46.350 --> 12:47.310
Did you come back

12:48.150 --> 12:49.850
Thanks to you, I finally came back

12:50.310 --> 12:51.230
Sorry

12:51.940 --> 12:55.020
I'm actually the one who wanted to do the parallel jump

12:56.270 --> 12:59.310
I want to go to a world where my parents are not divorced

13:01.400 --> 13:05.150
However, I alone cannot start the IP capsule

13:05.150 --> 13:07.150
So I want your help

13:07.980 --> 13:11.150
That's why, you let me make my wish come true first

13:11.770 --> 13:15.020
But, I didn't think about how to come back

13:15.350 --> 13:16.150
Sorry

13:17.310 --> 13:20.350
It's okay, I've seen Yuno anyway

13:20.650 --> 13:21.440
Did you see her?

13:21.980 --> 13:23.480
Um

13:24.060 --> 13:26.650
Thank goodness

13:27.810 --> 13:30.150
But, I can't figure it out

13:31.060 --> 13:31.730
What's up?

13:32.480 --> 13:34.810
About alive and dead

13:35.730 --> 13:39.230
Are you talking about life or not?

13:39.850 --> 13:42.020
Uh, so to speak

13:42.810 --> 13:46.850
However, the living Yuno is soft and warm

13:47.810 --> 13:50.810
But it's grave is cold and motionless

13:52.230 --> 13:54.060
Grandpa must also...

13:55.020 --> 13:56.980
Isn't that the true meaning of life

13:58.230 --> 14:02.600
To be alive means to be warm, to be able to play together

14:03.020 --> 14:05.380
When you die, you become cold

14:05.380 --> 14:08.980
The world is coming to an end It means

14:10.560 --> 14:12.270
Um...

14:12.600 --> 14:14.440
You mean the possibility already lost?

14:15.480 --> 14:16.690
Yes, the possibility

14:17.270 --> 14:20.020
Yuno's warmth temperature is her possibility

14:21.100 --> 14:23.600
Of alive and dead

14:24.060 --> 14:27.560
Their temperature difference should be the essence of life

14:29.400 --> 14:31.350
You are amazing

14:33.020 --> 14:34.230
You flatter me

14:34.480 --> 14:36.810
Then it's your turn next time

14:38.770 --> 14:41.900
Find your parents without the possibility of divorce

14:47.600 --> 14:50.650
Hey, how to start that

14:51.520 --> 14:52.730
Just click

14:52.730 --> 14:53.100
Ah?

14:54.060 --> 14:56.650
Somehow it started

14:59.730 --> 15:03.230
Forget it, I have successfully shifted to parallel world anyway.

15:03.600 --> 15:04.770
Just try it

15:09.600 --> 15:11.020
Then i'm going to close it

15:15.310 --> 15:18.940
Remember to pray well, don't think about mayonnaise with tuna filling

15:20.730 --> 15:23.230
I feel like you're a glutton

15:26.100 --> 15:27.150
I know

15:33.650 --> 15:36.150
What are you two doing

15:36.940 --> 15:38.560
Ah, that...

15:38.560 --> 15:39.560
Mother

15:43.940 --> 15:47.060
So your mother is the director

15:47.520 --> 15:48.060
Um

15:49.020 --> 15:53.060
Talking about parallel worlds is much longer than preaching

15:53.770 --> 15:57.350
As long as she's obsessed, she doesn't care about anything

15:59.600 --> 16:02.270
Aren't you the same in this regard

16:03.270 --> 16:05.190
As expected of a mother and daughter

16:06.400 --> 16:07.440
Not "you"

16:07.770 --> 16:08.350
What?

16:09.060 --> 16:11.190
My name is not "you"

16:14.900 --> 16:15.480
My name is Shiori

16:17.690 --> 16:18.690
Sato Shiori

16:20.440 --> 16:22.310
I'm Hidaka Koyomi

16:23.480 --> 16:25.230
Nice to meet you Koyomi

16:30.810 --> 16:31.850
Nice to

16:44.100 --> 16:47.190
August is full of fantasy

16:47.190 --> 16:49.940
We dried up

16:49.940 --> 16:52.980
Forget the heat and run

16:52.980 --> 16:56.060
No one can stop me

16:56.060 --> 16:59.150
With an innocent profile

16:59.150 --> 17:02.230
The sweat of blood that does not ooze

17:02.230 --> 17:06.190
The sticky hair and the voice of cicadas

17:06.190 --> 17:09.690
Both annoying and dearly

17:09.690 --> 17:15.100
I feel like I'm drowning in the summer sky

17:15.100 --> 17:19.100
Even though we're too blu

17:19.100 --> 17:22.560
It's good that you're still young

17:22.560 --> 17:24.560
The world is shrinkin

17:24.560 --> 17:29.270
The two of us would have nowhere to live

17:29.270 --> 17:35.440
I want to stick with you and stay closer to you

17:35.440 --> 17:39.690
While laughing, even if it's exaggerated

17:39.690 --> 17:46.020
Is it the sun that makes my face turn red?

17:46.020 --> 17:50.150
It's okay to keep it a secret

17:47.690 --> 17:49.270
I want to help others

17:51.020 --> 17:52.020
Help others

17:52.650 --> 17:54.520
Let's go find someone in trouble

17:56.100 --> 17:56.850
Fine

17:58.230 --> 17:59.190
Why so sudden?

17:59.690 --> 18:02.230
Because the summer vacation starts tomorrow

18:04.650 --> 18:06.060
You are not answering the question

18:07.060 --> 18:09.310
Don't you like to help others, Koyomi?

18:10.060 --> 18:10.440
No

18:11.350 --> 18:13.270
If those people are in trouble, I will definitely help them

18:14.480 --> 18:17.650
Right, then you have to look for it

18:19.100 --> 18:19.770
Yes Yes

18:34.100 --> 18:36.020
Can't find anyone in trouble?

18:38.690 --> 18:42.020
However, it is a good thing that everyone has no difficulties.

18:43.730 --> 18:44.650
yes

18:46.480 --> 18:49.350
But you, why do you think of helping others?

18:54.480 --> 18:55.520
i saw my dad

18:57.100 --> 18:58.400
first time after divorce

19:02.690 --> 19:05.310
My dad said he likes me the most

19:08.850 --> 19:12.520
He wants me to be a helpful person who doesn't ask for anything in return

19:13.980 --> 19:15.060
So you want to help others?

19:16.350 --> 19:16.770
Um

19:20.270 --> 19:23.940
After that, if I have difficulties, come and help me.

19:25.560 --> 19:27.850
What's wrong, don't you want to help me?

19:28.650 --> 19:30.230
because when i help you

19:30.850 --> 19:34.190
I can't say "It's a trivial matter, nothing to worry about"

19:34.690 --> 19:35.440
What?

19:35.900 --> 19:38.980
You don't ask for anything in return for helping others, don't you?

19:39.940 --> 19:41.310
help someone you don't know

19:41.650 --> 19:42.730
When those people ask your name

19:43.270 --> 19:46.690
Then you can say "It's a trivial matter, nothing to worry about"

19:47.690 --> 19:49.560
So i can't help you

19:52.480 --> 19:55.980
You are really stupid sometimes huh

19:57.150 --> 19:57.690
Why

19:59.440 --> 20:00.440
Why

20:20.150 --> 20:23.020
at night this place have a Great view

20:23.650 --> 20:24.350
Yeah

20:25.270 --> 20:26.650
i can see the lab from here

20:27.940 --> 20:29.810
but still a bit far

20:31.310 --> 20:32.230
Then let's try it

20:33.940 --> 20:37.100
Next time let's come here at night, when it's summer vacation

20:41.020 --> 20:41.900
Why next time?

20:42.480 --> 20:45.190
Because my tummy's so hungry

20:46.480 --> 20:47.100
yes

21:01.810 --> 21:05.020
It's still too tiring to help others every day

21:11.060 --> 21:12.440
uh, wait

21:12.440 --> 21:13.060
realy?

21:12.560 --> 21:17.560
I have something very important to say, remember to come to the institute at 11 o'clock.
Dad

21:15.810 --> 21:21.650
The science of imaginary matter must first establish the concept of imaginary space

21:23.190 --> 21:28.560
This world is formed by the interlacing of material space and imaginary space

21:28.560 --> 21:31.060
This is the basic assumption of fictional science

21:32.900 --> 21:35.690
Different from the material space composed of elementary particles

21:36.190 --> 21:39.520
Virtual space is composed of virtual elements

21:38.560 --> 21:39.650
You're here too, Shiori?

21:40.190 --> 21:43.190
The difference in its changes breeds parallel worlds

21:40.560 --> 21:41.650
mom asked me

21:43.900 --> 21:46.230
Although the phantom elements cannot be directly observed

21:44.810 --> 21:45.350
sorry

21:46.230 --> 21:46.810
um

21:46.810 --> 21:51.060
But its traces can be observed through the texture left by elementary particles

21:52.730 --> 21:54.520
This is the phantom pattern

21:55.900 --> 21:57.900
Imaginary Elements Print

21:58.560 --> 21:59.650
IP for short

22:00.150 --> 22:02.840
The current team headed by the deputy director of Hidaka

22:02.840 --> 22:05.060
Promoted a Digitalization of IP

22:06.350 --> 22:07.440
if written as a formula

22:09.940 --> 22:10.810
first...

22:11.770 --> 22:12.600
then...

22:15.150 --> 22:17.400
After quantifying the difference in IP

22:17.400 --> 22:19.190
to locate parallel worlds

22:20.190 --> 22:21.940
Suppose the current world is 0

22:22.310 --> 22:25.810
The larger the value, the farther away your parallel world is from here

22:26.520 --> 22:27.440
that's it

22:27.940 --> 22:28.810
So fine

22:29.270 --> 22:29.850
questions

22:30.600 --> 22:34.650
If successfuly located, can you jump to the parallel world you want to go?

22:35.150 --> 22:36.600
maybe in the future

22:37.600 --> 22:40.730
Although it is still in the stage of triggering the jump

22:42.020 --> 22:47.450
The original purpose of the IP capsule is to jump to a specific parallel world

22:47.450 --> 22:48.900
directional jump

22:50.810 --> 22:51.560
also

22:52.940 --> 22:55.440
Changes in virtual elements will breed time

22:56.600 --> 23:01.600
Time does not breed change, change itself is time

23:02.900 --> 23:04.940
That, that is to say...

23:05.650 --> 23:06.150
questions

23:07.190 --> 23:08.900
It's out of topic but

23:09.690 --> 23:13.100
Did you call us here to listen to classes?

23:15.600 --> 23:18.560
yeah, are this the important thing you want us to listen?

23:28.100 --> 23:32.100
Actually, I and Sato... Director...

23:34.400 --> 23:35.230
that…

23:36.060 --> 23:37.520
we plan to remarry

23:46.270 --> 23:47.270
I didn't know

23:48.020 --> 23:48.520
Um

23:49.730 --> 23:50.520
did you notice

23:51.060 --> 23:52.600
Absolutely not

23:53.120 --> 23:55.270
But I know they are college classmates

23:56.730 --> 23:57.980
I've heard of this too

23:59.440 --> 24:05.440
I don't mind your father being my father

24:06.480 --> 24:10.400
I don't mind the director being my mother

24:11.520 --> 24:11.980
But

24:13.150 --> 24:13.810
I..

24:15.350 --> 24:20.600
I've always had a hunch

24:22.940 --> 24:25.350
I think I will marry with you in the future

24:29.940 --> 24:33.270
But now it's no longer possible

24:34.190 --> 24:35.520
because we became brother and sister

24:44.060 --> 24:44.560
Shiori

24:49.690 --> 24:50.270
Let's run away

25:03.480 --> 25:04.350
Where do you want to go

25:06.310 --> 25:07.400
Anywhere is fine

25:08.100 --> 25:10.190
I can go anywhere as long as I'm with you

25:11.560 --> 25:12.810
How long shall we escape

25:14.310 --> 25:16.940
a week? a month?

25:18.400 --> 25:20.440
a year? ten years?

25:22.940 --> 25:25.060
Then i want to build a new home

25:26.940 --> 25:30.350
Fill it with favorite furniture

25:34.770 --> 25:35.940
I also want to build a garden

25:37.440 --> 25:38.730
Let's keep a dog in the yard

25:40.690 --> 25:43.310
raise it big and fluffy

25:45.900 --> 25:48.560
and someday when we grow up

25:49.400 --> 25:51.770
and someday we will get married

25:54.770 --> 25:57.980
But before that day comes

25:59.650 --> 26:00.980
Where should we go

26:20.270 --> 26:21.690
This is not okay

26:23.230 --> 26:23.690
Um

26:32.560 --> 26:34.440
I really want to grow up early

26:35.520 --> 26:36.850
What happened suddenly..

26:38.520 --> 26:41.520
When I grow up, I won't be scolded when I go out at night

26:42.940 --> 26:45.440
You won't do this if you'r a grown up

26:55.480 --> 26:57.350
You are right

26:59.560 --> 27:00.600
It's realy beautiful

27:06.520 --> 27:07.350
I had a dream

27:09.060 --> 27:09.520
a dreams?

27:10.730 --> 27:12.520
The future me comes to find me in my dream

27:14.310 --> 27:15.520
The future me said

27:16.350 --> 27:19.270
"Even if I grow up and become an old woman"

27:20.020 --> 27:21.940
"I've been with you forever"

27:23.690 --> 27:24.230
Yeah

27:25.400 --> 27:28.020
She also said, "Became a grandpa's dumbfounded"

27:28.600 --> 27:30.690
"As if to forget me"

27:32.020 --> 27:35.150
"If that's the case, I'll help you, Koyomi"

27:36.020 --> 27:38.520
"And then say, 'It's a trivial matter, nothing to worry about'"

27:41.480 --> 27:44.440
You must have been confused earlier than me

27:45.690 --> 27:49.270
Will you come and help me then ?

27:50.650 --> 27:50.980
OK

27:51.690 --> 27:52.230
Really?

27:54.810 --> 27:55.650
I promise

27:56.480 --> 27:59.440
As long as you encounter difficulties, I will definitely help you

28:05.650 --> 28:07.440
It would be great if it could be done

28:09.230 --> 28:09.770
must be able to

28:10.850 --> 28:15.600
That dream must have been transferred to you from a parallel world

28:15.980 --> 28:18.480
No, then it won't be from the old you

28:19.730 --> 28:20.350
Found it

28:21.770 --> 28:22.230
What?

28:22.770 --> 28:24.150
Place we can escape

28:25.400 --> 28:25.940
Where?

28:26.900 --> 28:28.100
In parallel world

28:29.560 --> 28:33.100
There must be a world where our parents didn't get divorced

28:35.190 --> 28:35.770
Yes

28:36.730 --> 28:40.060
There, my father and the director will not remarry

28:40.400 --> 28:42.480
We won't be brother and sister

28:43.310 --> 28:44.600
Let's go, Shiori

28:45.060 --> 28:45.440
Um

28:52.850 --> 28:55.850
When we get to a parallel world, where can we meet?

28:57.900 --> 29:01.150
At that place where we can see a good night view

29:03.150 --> 29:03.650
OK

29:16.270 --> 29:17.770
what's wrong

29:18.810 --> 29:20.230
It's so narrow, I can't help it

29:21.150 --> 29:21.650
Um

29:22.440 --> 29:25.520
I thought you'd be facing the other way

29:26.770 --> 29:27.400
I'll turn around now

29:27.400 --> 29:27.940
No

29:30.810 --> 29:33.400
No need, that's fine

29:36.810 --> 29:37.440
I see

29:44.100 --> 29:45.150
We would wishing right?

29:46.600 --> 29:47.020
Um

29:48.100 --> 29:51.520
I was just wishing and shifted

29:54.270 --> 29:58.480
Then, can I wish to marry you?

29:59.520 --> 30:00.060
Sure

30:00.900 --> 30:04.020
I will also wish to be with you

30:06.270 --> 30:07.060
Koyomi

30:08.850 --> 30:11.770
Make me as your wife in a parallel world

30:12.900 --> 30:13.400
Um

30:15.980 --> 30:18.480
Let's get married in a parallel world

30:42.850 --> 30:43.730
Mother?

30:54.020 --> 30:54.650
Shiori

31:06.350 --> 31:08.770
Why, why is mom at home?

31:09.600 --> 31:10.900
Why

31:11.650 --> 31:12.150
Am i not?

31:13.100 --> 31:13.650
But..

31:15.400 --> 31:18.480
Is there any problem staying at her own home?

31:19.690 --> 31:20.650
Home?

31:23.600 --> 31:24.480
What's wrong

31:24.480 --> 31:26.310
You two are not divorced, are you?

31:34.900 --> 31:37.440
mom and dad

31:39.350 --> 31:40.150
What's wrong

31:41.100 --> 31:43.150
mom and dad

31:43.440 --> 31:44.350
Wait.

31:44.350 --> 31:46.520
You were talking nonsense just now, where are you going now?

31:46.520 --> 31:47.900
sorry i'm in a hurry

31:49.520 --> 31:50.480
I succeeded

31:51.480 --> 31:53.480
I want to see Shiori, hurry up and see Shiori

31:56.850 --> 31:57.650
I want to see Shiori quickly

32:10.900 --> 32:11.730
Koyomi

32:21.560 --> 32:23.600
What, I turned out to be back here

32:25.400 --> 32:27.230
After it went so smoothly

32:31.020 --> 32:33.560
Hey, wake up, Shiori

32:34.730 --> 32:37.150
The observation accuracy of IP seems to be not very good

32:37.730 --> 32:41.940
Values cannot be derived without detailed data

32:42.980 --> 32:44.350
let's try to find a helper

32:44.650 --> 32:45.850
From college classmate?

32:46.400 --> 32:50.730
I think his name is kawa... waka...

32:52.940 --> 32:53.480
What's wrong

32:54.020 --> 32:54.730
Nothing

32:58.560 --> 33:00.600
Is there anyone? Is there anyone?

33:01.600 --> 33:02.560
Help me

33:04.520 --> 33:05.230
Koyomi?

33:06.480 --> 33:07.060
Shiori?

33:07.850 --> 33:09.810
Dad, Shiori...

33:10.480 --> 33:12.310
What are you doing

33:12.310 --> 33:15.230
She's... she's not breathing

33:28.150 --> 33:28.810
Shiori

33:29.900 --> 33:30.770
How is she?

33:34.810 --> 33:36.480
Her heart still beating

33:37.230 --> 33:40.690
Precisely, and artificially beating

33:43.400 --> 33:44.730
she didn't regain consciousness

33:47.770 --> 33:48.940
and in a coma

33:56.600 --> 33:57.650
sorry

33:58.230 --> 34:00.560
I didn't realize your intentions

34:01.850 --> 34:05.150
But you misunderstood one thing

34:07.020 --> 34:08.730
Even if the parents of both parties remarried

34:09.440 --> 34:11.730
Children can still marry

34:13.690 --> 34:16.980
So you don't have to run away

34:59.020 --> 34:59.900
Koyomi

35:01.270 --> 35:01.980
Shiori?

35:03.810 --> 35:04.480
Sorry

35:05.150 --> 35:08.270
I turned into a ghost

35:10.850 --> 35:13.810
Virtual Element Mitosis

35:14.850 --> 35:18.350
Let's name Shiori's state like this

35:19.690 --> 35:21.940
Although it seems to be in a state of coma

35:22.310 --> 35:26.100
But her brain didn't suffer any damage

35:27.230 --> 35:29.230
It just stops working

35:30.650 --> 35:35.020
I don't think it's an effect of parallel worlds

35:36.650 --> 35:37.440
Keep talking

35:38.230 --> 35:42.020
If the assumption that "Ghost Shiori is at the crossroads" that Koyomi said is true

35:44.100 --> 35:47.400
So Shiori had an accident in a parallel world

35:47.900 --> 35:49.850
Then shift to the original world

35:50.690 --> 35:54.560
But her body in the parallel world died later

35:55.600 --> 36:00.060
Her void lost the body it was attached to and disappeared

36:01.310 --> 36:04.810
In this way, Shiori lost his virtual substance and physical body.

36:05.560 --> 36:07.480
So she became a ghost at the crossroads

36:08.900 --> 36:14.900
It turns out that the time of physical death and parallel shift coincides

36:16.060 --> 36:18.400
Blame us for unauthorized use of IP capsules

36:20.190 --> 36:21.560
It was just an accident

36:23.060 --> 36:26.980
Besides, that IP capsule cannot perform parallel shift

36:28.730 --> 36:29.810
It's not finished

36:31.190 --> 36:31.650
But...

36:32.020 --> 36:36.650
You said you've successfully performed a parallel shift before?

36:37.310 --> 36:39.900
That's probably because of your physique

36:40.690 --> 36:43.770
May be a constitution prone to parallel shift

36:45.350 --> 36:46.770
Am I this type of physique?

36:47.190 --> 36:48.060
That's it

36:48.440 --> 36:50.230
The void is always shaking

36:51.150 --> 36:55.690
If the amplitude exceeds a certain limit, it will cause a parallel shift

36:56.350 --> 37:01.060
If the amplitude is already large, it is easy to cause shift

37:01.520 --> 37:03.770
What if the amplitude could be controlled?

37:04.560 --> 37:07.020
It might be possible to achieve a directional shift

37:07.850 --> 37:10.690
Is it possible that Shiori has the same physique?

37:11.400 --> 37:14.600
Only You can see Shiori, could this be the reason...

37:14.600 --> 37:15.560
Is she still savable?

37:21.480 --> 37:23.600
Is there a way to save Shiori?

37:26.650 --> 37:30.020
As long as we can observe and control Shiori's virtual elements

37:30.520 --> 37:34.190
And fixed it in the original substance - her flesh

37:34.190 --> 37:35.600
Maybe there's a chance

37:36.900 --> 37:40.900
But the virtual element is only a theoretical existence, and it cannot be observed yet

37:41.480 --> 37:43.770
Then please use me as a test subject

37:44.560 --> 37:46.770
Just investigate me thoroughly, that can shift easly

37:47.100 --> 37:48.400
Maybe we can figure it out

37:49.850 --> 37:50.560
Koyomi

37:51.690 --> 37:54.190
Shiori became like this, it's all my fault

37:55.150 --> 37:58.020
Because I'm too stupid, too ignorant

37:59.480 --> 38:00.440
That's why she...

38:03.020 --> 38:05.230
As I said earlier, it was just an accident

38:05.980 --> 38:06.480
Anyone...

38:08.560 --> 38:11.100
I can do anything, please help Shiori

38:11.400 --> 38:12.100
Calm down

38:12.100 --> 38:13.900
How can i calm down

38:14.520 --> 38:17.560
But you guys, why are you still so calm?

38:20.900 --> 38:23.190
Mad at me

38:24.100 --> 38:25.690
Why don't you beat me and scold me?

38:26.440 --> 38:29.600
Are you not sad at all when your daughter is lying on the hospital bed?

38:45.100 --> 38:45.770
Koyomi

38:46.270 --> 38:47.440
It's okay Hidaka

38:48.690 --> 38:51.060
It's also my fault that I can only keep thinking

38:52.810 --> 38:55.900
I'm such a good-for-nothing mother

38:57.350 --> 38:58.690
Me too

38:59.520 --> 39:03.400
Sorry, but I really want to do something for Shiori

39:04.560 --> 39:07.560
Please, let me help to

39:09.400 --> 39:12.600
No, if an accident happens to you too

39:12.600 --> 39:14.520
I'm counting on you too, Sato

39:16.810 --> 39:17.600
Hidaka

39:18.020 --> 39:18.520
Dad

39:20.350 --> 39:26.940
At least let my worthless father bear it with his son

39:32.560 --> 39:33.230
All right

39:35.020 --> 39:35.560
But

39:36.100 --> 39:38.560
You have to finish your studies well first

39:39.210 --> 39:41.980
Also cherish your own life

39:44.900 --> 39:49.850
I go to classes at school during the day and to Lab to study at night

39:51.270 --> 39:55.560
In order not to let the tragedy happen again, I tried my best to learn all kinds of knowledge

39:57.100 --> 40:01.520
Because of this, I was admitted to a prestigious school in the county with the first place

40:04.810 --> 40:08.650
Even if the evening goes and the morning comes, I still insist on visiting Shiori every day

40:13.230 --> 40:16.350
Parallel-shifting clinical trials run late at night

40:17.900 --> 40:20.600
This is to avoid accidents like Shiori's

40:23.560 --> 40:26.350
Although dozens of clinical trials

40:26.980 --> 40:29.850
However, the observation of virtual elements has still not progressed.

40:32.690 --> 40:35.190
But there's only one thing I know

40:37.310 --> 40:40.560
No matter in which parallel world, Shiori is in the form of a ghost

40:42.600 --> 40:45.730
There is no world in which Shiori can be saved

40:51.060 --> 40:51.810
Koyomi

40:54.150 --> 40:57.730
Shiori, I'm from a parallel world

40:59.350 --> 41:00.100
Yeah

41:01.900 --> 41:04.400
Me at this moment and me in this world

41:05.110 --> 41:06.060
is there any difference

41:10.150 --> 41:12.440
I don't understand, it looks exactly the same

41:14.770 --> 41:15.350
Yeah

41:21.690 --> 41:22.440
The pigeons will fly

41:23.350 --> 41:23.810
Pigeon?

41:24.270 --> 41:24.770
Um

41:25.440 --> 41:26.730
From bronze statue over there

41:29.020 --> 41:31.900
From time to time it stands there during the day

41:37.270 --> 41:38.850
Maybe it's waiting for a companion

41:54.350 --> 41:56.770
Koyomi, the last train is coming soon.

41:59.100 --> 42:00.230
Ah. There is something I want to do

42:00.690 --> 42:03.190
Really, then remember to close the doors and windows

42:04.440 --> 42:05.270
I go first then

42:06.150 --> 42:07.100
You two worked hard

42:12.400 --> 42:13.690
So cold

42:14.410 --> 42:16.690
Even in warm winter, the nights are cold

42:17.020 --> 42:19.510
You must have worked too hard

42:19.980 --> 42:21.480
I didn't seem to come home yesterday

42:22.020 --> 42:24.320
It's good for young people to work hard

42:24.820 --> 42:27.230
For Japan and us old bones

42:27.770 --> 42:29.850
Forget us old bones

42:30.270 --> 42:33.100
Do you want to tell the director before he breaks down?

42:33.810 --> 42:35.980
The director went to Fukuoka the day before yesterday

42:36.940 --> 42:37.690
and..

42:40.270 --> 42:42.230
I can't understand his feeling

42:52.480 --> 42:53.350
It's not right

42:54.190 --> 42:56.480
In this way, the scope will be infinitely expanded

43:05.150 --> 43:08.520
The same event is sure to happen worldwide

43:10.810 --> 43:13.350
The gravity of the ground...

43:31.690 --> 43:32.480
Where it is?

43:46.810 --> 43:47.770
Are you awake

43:50.100 --> 43:50.730
Koyomi

44:21.600 --> 44:22.190
Koyomi

44:24.650 --> 44:25.230
Dad

44:26.350 --> 44:28.350
You'r still here, are you staying up late?

44:29.980 --> 44:31.150
Come with me

44:32.190 --> 44:32.770
Where?

44:34.850 --> 44:36.730
The director just called me

44:40.060 --> 44:42.940
Shiori's heart stopped beating

45:52.730 --> 45:53.440
Koyomi

45:54.850 --> 45:57.150
Sorry for not being able to come this time

45:58.020 --> 46:00.270
It's okay.

46:02.980 --> 46:04.730
Did something sad happen?

46:05.730 --> 46:06.400
uh no

46:11.270 --> 46:11.980
Looks like

46:13.550 --> 46:16.770
You just separated from someone forever

46:21.350 --> 46:22.230
Koyomi-kun?

46:25.690 --> 46:27.850
It's okay, it's okay

46:28.520 --> 46:29.700
I was always here

46:30.510 --> 46:32.600
I will always be with you

46:33.150 --> 46:33.560
Okay

46:35.850 --> 46:36.480
Shiori

46:41.770 --> 46:43.270
Why, Shiori?

46:44.400 --> 46:45.100
Why?

46:51.270 --> 46:52.810
By the way, that pigeon...

47:31.400 --> 47:33.150
it hurts

47:34.150 --> 47:35.650
Eh, sleep until noon?

47:36.900 --> 47:38.730
I was going to take a nap tho

47:41.100 --> 47:43.560
I really can't do anything about you, Koyomi

47:44.350 --> 47:46.060
You have no right to say that

47:49.400 --> 47:51.350
ah, what do you mean

47:51.060 --> 47:52.270
What are you looking at

47:53.520 --> 47:55.020
The director came here huh

47:55.980 --> 47:57.980
Maybe received an invitation from the Munich Academy

47:58.990 --> 48:00.310
Did she say something?

48:13.980 --> 48:14.520
Assistant?

48:15.100 --> 48:18.690
It was recommended by Sato's mentor when he was studying abroad

48:19.270 --> 48:20.480
Is it from Munich?

48:21.440 --> 48:23.650
In addition to being recommended by the Academy, I heard she also passed the interview

48:24.230 --> 48:26.520
She's a genius who completed a Ph.D

48:27.310 --> 48:27.810
Yeah

48:28.560 --> 48:29.980
But I don't need an assistant

48:31.650 --> 48:34.730
It seems that you don't want to explore the field of research

48:38.900 --> 48:40.060
I am sure she can help

48:40.980 --> 48:43.100
Even if it's just an extra person, it will be different

48:43.850 --> 48:46.560
How is it possible, besides, the other party is older than me

48:47.230 --> 48:48.230
I must be polite or...

48:48.230 --> 48:49.150
We are in the same school year

48:50.850 --> 48:54.020
I was born in March, and my birthday is counted one year later

48:57.150 --> 48:58.190
And that's what she say

49:00.100 --> 49:01.610
I'm Takigawa Kazune

49:02.330 --> 49:05.060
Nice to meet with you, Chief Hidaka

49:07.560 --> 49:09.310
I said that alone is more comfortable

49:09.980 --> 49:11.770
It's hard to concentrate when there are too many people

49:12.440 --> 49:15.100
Mentoring a juniors is also the Chief is job

49:15.350 --> 49:18.020
Mentoring? Me a high school mentoring a Ph.D ?

49:18.600 --> 49:20.190
She came by herself

49:22.020 --> 49:22.730
Director

49:23.650 --> 49:27.690
Presumably to the young scientists who advocated the "inescapable event radius"

49:28.060 --> 49:29.480
interest ?

49:30.980 --> 49:32.150
Please stop

49:35.560 --> 49:36.940
I won't force you

49:37.440 --> 49:40.770
But one cannot live alone

49:42.480 --> 49:45.810
As a parent, you must worry about your son

49:47.100 --> 49:50.480
Mom, you're too cunning

49:51.560 --> 49:53.350
Leave work on time today

49:53.350 --> 49:56.100
Let's go to a celebratory meal with her

49:56.690 --> 49:58.150
Too much trouble

49:58.980 --> 50:01.100
Well, remember to take a shower before going to eat

50:01.480 --> 50:02.770
Hey, is it that dirty?

50:03.230 --> 50:04.440
Shave your mustache and change clothes

50:04.900 --> 50:06.480
Don't wear the usual UNIQLO shirt

50:09.980 --> 50:12.190
Is it really okay in here?

50:12.600 --> 50:12.980
Um

50:14.230 --> 50:16.150
Well, do you want something to eat?

50:16.150 --> 50:16.650
No

50:17.900 --> 50:19.850
so do you want to sing

50:20.270 --> 50:20.650
No

50:22.850 --> 50:23.850
Yeah

50:27.060 --> 50:28.560
Then why come to karaoke

50:29.520 --> 50:32.230
Because the environment here is suitable for conversation

50:32.900 --> 50:33.560
Conversation?

50:34.060 --> 50:35.060
Before that

50:37.230 --> 50:38.770
Can you stop using polite language

50:40.060 --> 50:41.730
We are in the same school year, right?

50:42.100 --> 50:44.600
No, a classmate

50:45.270 --> 50:46.020
Classmate?

50:47.020 --> 50:48.940
You really don't remember

50:49.480 --> 50:51.020
Your delicacies are too less

50:51.600 --> 50:52.310
Thats..

50:52.310 --> 50:55.060
Aren't you a freshman representative?

50:56.810 --> 50:59.850
We are high school classmates

51:01.100 --> 51:02.810
But looks like you don't remember

51:04.520 --> 51:07.190
Because I often leave early in high school

51:08.520 --> 51:10.520
But your grades are always number one

51:10.940 --> 51:12.520
I've never been first

51:15.270 --> 51:17.900
I wanted to get it back in college

51:18.600 --> 51:21.400
But you are the first person to enter virtual science

51:21.400 --> 51:23.400
Dr. Sato's Institute

51:24.730 --> 51:28.520
No matter how good you are, it is impossible for high school students to get in

51:29.770 --> 51:30.650
I was disappointed

51:32.520 --> 51:34.640
I thought you came in through the back door

51:34.640 --> 51:35.400
Thats...

51:35.400 --> 51:36.400
But i was wrong

51:38.650 --> 51:42.900
A few years later, you came up with the "Radius of Unavoidable Events"

51:43.520 --> 51:45.980
And be the forefront of virtual science

51:47.400 --> 51:49.020
You do have a real talents

51:51.480 --> 51:55.600
No, that's just a by-product of the parallel shift experiment

51:55.810 --> 51:56.600
What an annoying

52:00.310 --> 52:02.730
When I was studying abroad, I completed the doctoral program at the fastest speed

52:03.020 --> 52:05.270
Then passed the interview of Dr. Sato and joined the Institute

52:05.600 --> 52:07.230
From now on we will be on the same field

52:07.560 --> 52:08.310
Be aware

52:14.230 --> 52:16.810
Forget it, I've calmed down a bit.

52:31.900 --> 52:34.310
Hey, sing something

52:38.730 --> 52:40.100
Hey. Are you okay?

52:40.100 --> 52:43.650
nothing, nothing, I'm fine.

52:45.980 --> 52:47.650
Fast up faster

52:50.770 --> 52:52.480
Nice timing

52:52.480 --> 52:53.400
Obviously out

52:54.350 --> 52:55.560
Let's go there next

53:15.350 --> 53:16.020
I'll come here soon

53:17.150 --> 53:17.650
Um

53:18.270 --> 53:18.810
Huh?

53:20.440 --> 53:21.770
Can you see it too

53:22.440 --> 53:24.020
Ghost at the crossroads

53:25.690 --> 53:28.900
Haven't heard of it? It's an urban legend.

53:29.150 --> 53:31.440
I can see it every now and then

53:33.100 --> 53:34.310
Can you see of what?

53:35.850 --> 53:40.690
I can vaguely see the shadow of a human figure

53:41.810 --> 53:42.770
Only by chance

53:45.350 --> 53:45.850
Follow me

53:47.980 --> 53:49.100
Wait, what are you doing

53:50.310 --> 53:52.060
What's up?

54:23.520 --> 54:25.770
Virtual Element Mitosis

54:26.690 --> 54:27.650
I see

54:28.310 --> 54:31.900
I entered the research institute to save Shiori

54:33.400 --> 54:34.940
To fixed IP's

54:36.060 --> 54:36.770
For example if

54:37.190 --> 54:39.650
Deputy director research about IP's lock

54:40.440 --> 54:44.350
Although it can fix the void and prevent parallel jumping

54:45.060 --> 54:49.020
If you use it well, it might sink her emptiness

54:49.690 --> 54:51.810
Then assimilate the void and the flesh will...

54:51.810 --> 54:54.600
Shiori's body is gone

54:56.150 --> 54:59.020
After persisted in coma for several years, she still couldn't hold on

55:07.350 --> 55:08.440
What are you going to do then?

55:09.940 --> 55:13.900
If you insist on staying in the institute, you should have something on your minds right?

55:17.690 --> 55:20.310
I know, that's why you are called genius

55:21.520 --> 55:22.980
Your delicacies are too less...

55:22.980 --> 55:25.650
I'm researching the time shift

55:27.400 --> 55:32.600
To send Shiori's virtual substance to a world beyond the "radius of the event that encountered the accident"

55:33.650 --> 55:36.730
Let her shift to the point where this world diverges from that world

55:38.980 --> 55:42.060
However, time shifting is theoretically impossible

55:42.270 --> 55:45.230
That's right, so I can't get the budget

55:46.480 --> 55:50.770
Misappropriating research expenses huh, no wonder you are obsessed with researching it alone

55:52.150 --> 55:54.940
I will save Shiori no matter what

55:56.190 --> 55:57.900
She's still at that crossroads

55:58.560 --> 56:01.480
No one can notice her

56:04.520 --> 56:07.150
That accident ruined Shiori's possibilities

56:07.850 --> 56:12.400
So I'm going to let the cause of the accident never exist in the first place

56:16.190 --> 56:18.350
I tell you this because you can see Shiori

56:19.100 --> 56:20.230
Can you keep it a secret

56:22.060 --> 56:23.560
Let me turn a blind eye

56:24.230 --> 56:24.850
Please

56:30.060 --> 56:31.020
I won't turn a blind eye

56:32.480 --> 56:34.940
Unless you let me research it with you

56:35.730 --> 56:40.650
I want to have a race with you to see who can shifting time first

56:41.100 --> 56:42.190
That is the condition

56:45.400 --> 56:47.690
Okay, pleased to work with you, Takigawa-san

56:48.230 --> 56:49.850
Please take care of me, Hidaka-kun

56:50.600 --> 56:51.980
Hidaka-kun, huh

56:52.000 --> 56:54.980
My dad and director also call me that

56:55.690 --> 56:57.980
You can call me Koyomi, that's what everyone calls me

56:58.400 --> 57:00.230
Then you also call me Kazune

57:05.980 --> 57:07.480
Nice to meet you, Koyomi

57:15.350 --> 57:16.600
Are you awake

57:19.060 --> 57:20.060
Koyomi

57:27.020 --> 57:27.770
What's wrong

57:29.190 --> 57:29.770
Nothing

57:30.520 --> 57:31.900
Nice to meet you, Kazune

